# 05 — Cell Characterization, Timing and Congestion

## 📌 Introduction

Standard cells must be characterized before they can be effectively used in ASIC design.

Characterization determines the electrical and timing behavior of a cell under different operating conditions.

This section introduces the cell design flow, characterization flow, timing thresholds, propagation delay, transition time and congestion-aware placement.

